  <!-- FAQ Section -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <h2 class="section__title">Private Label Clothing FAQ</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What is private label clothing manufacturing?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Private label clothing manufacturing involves a manufacturer producing garments that are sold under your brand name. You select from pre-designed or semi-custom styles, apply your branding through labels, tags, and packaging, and sell the finished products as your own. This model balances customization with speed, allowing brands to launch collections without the complexity of full custom design from scratch.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How is private label different from custom manufacturing?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Private label uses existing designs that you brand as your own, while custom manufacturing involves creating garments entirely from your original designs. Private label is faster and cheaper because patterns and tech packs already exist. Custom manufacturing offers complete design control but requires longer development time, higher costs, and larger minimum orders. Private label is ideal for startups testing the market, while custom suits established brands with specific design visions.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What are the benefits of private label clothing?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Private label clothing offers five key benefits: speed to market with collections launching in weeks rather than months, lower startup costs by eliminating pattern-making and tech pack expenses, easier product testing with smaller quantities, scalability as you can grow from private label to semi-custom with the same manufacturer, brand ownership with complete control over your identity and customer relationships, and lower risk with smaller initial investments.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What can I customize in private label clothing?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Private label customization options include branded woven labels and hang tags, custom neck labels with your logo, screen print or embroidery placement, fabric color selection from available options, size range adjustments, packaging customization with branded boxes or bags, trim modifications like drawstrings or buttons, and logo placement on specific garment areas. Advanced customization includes custom fabric sourcing and fit adjustments for larger orders.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What is the minimum order quantity for private label clothing?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Private label MOQs typically range from 100-500 pieces per style depending on the manufacturer and product type. SDF Clothing offers 300-piece minimums per style for private label production, making it accessible for startups and growing brands. Lower MOQs than custom manufacturing enable testing without large inventory commitments. Some manufacturers offer tiered pricing where per-unit costs decrease at higher quantity tiers.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How long does private label production take?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Private label production timeline typically ranges from 4-8 weeks from order placement to delivery. Sampling takes 1-2 weeks including revisions, bulk production adds 3-4 weeks for most orders, and shipping adds 1-2 weeks depending on destination. This is significantly faster than custom manufacturing which can take 8-12 weeks or more. The exact timeline depends on order size, customization complexity, and manufacturer capacity. SDF Clothing provides detailed production schedules for every order.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How much does private label clothing cost?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Private label costs vary by product type, fabric quality, customization level, and quantity. Basic t-shirts may cost $5-15 per piece, hoodies $15-30, and premium pieces $30-50 at manufacturer FOB pricing. Setup fees for labels and branding typically add $200-500. Sampling costs are usually credited against bulk orders. Total landed cost includes freight, duties, and local delivery. SDF Clothing provides transparent FOB quotes with no hidden fees.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Can I switch from private label to custom manufacturing?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Yes, many brands start with private label and transition to custom manufacturing as they grow. Private label allows testing market demand with minimal risk. Once you establish which styles sell and understand your customer preferences, you can move to semi-custom or fully custom production with the same manufacturer. This gradual scaling approach reduces risk while building toward fully custom collections. SDF Clothing supports brands through this growth trajectory with flexible <a href="/oem-clothing-manufacturer">OEM clothing manufacturer</a> options.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

